  "details": "https://youtu.be/MvmhvxQD_7M\n\nAs demonstrated in the video, there is a massive delay and dropped OSC packets when OSCQuery is used to advertise the port.\n\nThere seems to be some sort or caching method because there is always three packets delivered at a time and In a seemingly random order of arrival when compared to the repeatable order found in the direct connection. This makes OSCQuery based haptics practically unusable, since more often than not it doesn't catch the 0 (exiting) packet and leaves the haptics running at somewhere near full-tilt. This also means that any sort of trigger that doesn't last over a few seconds at a fairly high value doesn't allow the haptic motors to spin up and it only gets a few millisecond spike when the cached values are finally processed.\n\nThis has been tested on both the current beta build and the main distribution.",
